@startuml
title SEQ-08 - Paddle Checkout, Webhook Fulfillment and Access
autonumber
actor User
boundary Web
control Gateway as "Frontend Gateway"
control Core
participant Paddle
database DB as "core billing"
control GotIt

User -> Web: Choose paid plan
Web -> Core: POST /billing/checkout\nBearer + Idempotency-Key + planKey
Core -> DB: Authenticate user and load active plan
critical Checkout idempotency
  Core -> DB: Lock/create checkout attempt
  Core -> Paddle: Create scoped hosted transaction
  Paddle --> Core: transactionId + checkout URL
  Core -> DB: Save provider transaction/reference
end
Core --> Web: hosted URL
Web -> Gateway: GET /runtime-config
Gateway --> Web: public Paddle token/environment/price IDs
Web -> Paddle: Open checkout overlay
User -> Paddle: Payment/confirmation
Paddle --> User: Provider result
Paddle -> Core: POST /billing/webhooks/paddle\nraw body + signature
Core -> Core: Verify exact raw-body signature
break Invalid signature
  Core --> Paddle: non-2xx for retry/security
end
critical Idempotent fulfillment
  Core -> DB: Lock webhook event ID
  alt Duplicate successfully processed
    Core --> Paddle: duplicate acknowledgement
  else New/retryable event
    Core -> Core: Reject stale lifecycle transition
    Core -> DB: Upsert customer/subscription/transaction projection
    Core -> DB: Mark event processed/failed
  end
end
Core --> Paddle: 2xx processed/ignored/duplicate
Web -> Core: GET /billing/status
Core -> DB: Derive paid/trial/free and entitlements
Core --> Web: status
Web -> GotIt: Product mutation
GotIt -> Core: GET billing/status for guarded capability
Core --> GotIt: entitlements
GotIt --> Web: allowed or SUBSCRIPTION_REQUIRED
@enduml

